<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Betar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fell 135</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Bethar, Beitar (ancient)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Betar was an ancient fortified town in the Judaean hills south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, at Khirbet al-Yahud near the village of Battir. It was the last stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bar-kokhba">Simon bar Kokhba</a> in the revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and its fall in 135 CE ended the rising. Jewish tradition dates its capture to the fast of the Ninth of Av.</p></div>
